WEBVTT

00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:11.367
The Datadog plugin and connector let Claude query Datadog logs, metrics, traces, dashboards and monitors through the Datadog MCP Server.

00:00:11.933 --> 00:00:23.567
The Datadog MCP Server links your observability data to any agent that speaks the Model Context Protocol, so you ask instead of clicking through screens.

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:28.067
Claude, including Cowork, uses the official connector.

00:00:28.067 --> 00:00:33.367
Claude Code installs the plugin from the official Anthropic marketplace.

00:00:33.933 --> 00:00:37.467
Choose your Datadog site and sign in with OAuth.

00:00:37.467 --> 00:00:44.133
Keys are supported, and older manual servers or custom connectors should be removed first.

00:00:44.667 --> 00:00:52.800
You need Datadog permissions for the resources you query, and no Datadog credentials are sent to the model provider.

00:00:53.367 --> 00:01:01.633
Enable or disable groups of MCP tools so the agent sees only the Datadog products your team needs.

00:01:02.167 --> 00:01:03.933
The plugin is in Preview.

00:01:03.933 --> 00:01:12.067
The server is HIPAA-eligible, but you own compliance for connected tools, and the government sites are unsupported.
